WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:04.970
Wonder Woman is a big deal these days, but
there are some aspects of her history that

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.160
DC is definitely not in a hurry to acknowledge.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:11.380
Whether outdated or just a little too weird
for the mainstream, these elements sometimes

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.120
get swept under the proverbial rug.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.660
Her creator’s unusual beliefs

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:21.000
Wonder Woman's co-creator, with artist Harry
G. Peter, was William Moulton Marston, a psychologist

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.960
who was also responsible for the principles
behind the lie detector.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:28.180
His wife, Elizabeth Holloway Marston, is said
to be responsible for giving him the idea

00:00:28.189 --> 00:00:32.890
of a female superhero—and that superhero,
Wonder Woman, was visually inspired in part

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:37.870
by their girlfriend and third spouse, Olive
Byrne, right down to the metal cuff bracelets

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:38.620
she liked to wear.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:43.880
“And all her friends and helpers are sorority
girls who have spanking parties and fight

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:46.040
Germans and rides in an invisible plane."

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:47.220
"Yes.”

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:51.380
At the time, the trio would be considered
radical feminists, believing that women not

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:54.800
only deserved freedom to pursue their own
lives and pleasure, but were better suited

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:55.640
to run the world.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.720
They attended meetings at the home of Carolyn
Keatley, who led what some might call a feminist

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:00.340
sex cult.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:05.300
In time, Marston fathered children with both
Holloway and Byrne, and when he died in the

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:09.400
1950s, the two mothers continued to live together
and raise those children as a family.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:13.840
. Marston's interest in bondage and "loving
submission" had a funny way of making into

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:14.920
the comics he wrote.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:19.980
Couple that with his... unique living arrangement,
and you can see why DC isn't exactly promoting

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:20.920
that little factoid..

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:22.660
That doesn’t mean it’s a secret, though.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:27.740
The comics are well known for seeming pretty
kinky in retrospect, and the 2017 film Professor

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:30.660
Marston and the Wonder Women attempted to
tell the whole story.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:32.620
Secret identity theft

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:37.080
Most people know that Wonder Woman's secret
identity, when she bothers to have one, is

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:37.880
Diana Prince.

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:42.320
Since her real identity is Princess Diana,
you might assume she got her American alias

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:46.980
just by flipping that around, but in Sensation
Comics #1, she went about it a little differently.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:51.480
Arriving at a military hospital, Diana comes
upon a weeping nurse who happens to look just

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:51.980
like her.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:56.440
It turns out the nurse is actually named Diana
Prince, and she's crying because her fiancé

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:59.420
has found work in South America and she has
no money to join him.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:04.100
Wonder Woman has just earned a pile of cash
by demonstrating her Amazon abilities onstage,

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:08.300
so the real Diana Prince sells Princess Diana
her credentials and leaves the country.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:12.180
Since Wonder Woman was trained in nursing
on Paradise Island, this deception isn't a

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:13.480
problem for her patients.

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:17.720
However, she's also an undocumented immigrant
who got a job with the military using somebody

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:19.340
else's paperwork, which…

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:19.980
yeah.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.020
Um. let's just move on, shall we?.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.440
The Justice Society’s secretary

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:28.960
The Justice Society of America was the first
superhero team in comics and the predecessor

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:29.920
to the Justice League.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:34.960
Unsurprisingly for 1940, the team was entirely
male to start with, although the original

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:39.800
Red Tornado, a middle-aged housewife who became
a gender-ambiguous comedy hero, made an appearance

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:42.060
at their first meeting in All-Star Comics
#3.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:45.480
Nine issues later, they welcomed their newest
ally, Wonder Woman.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:46.560
As their secretary.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:51.160
World War II was in full swing, and the Society
had just been commissioned by President Roosevelt

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:54.860
to become an official part of the war effort,
so it made sense that they might need someone

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:56.240
to take minutes at their meetings.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:00.300
It makes no sense, however, that the job should
go to a trained warrior who's arguably more

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.920
powerful than anyone on the team.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:05.460
Fortunately, the secretary aspect of her membership
was quickly dropped.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:07.700
That Egg supervillain

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:13.000
During the cold war, evil communists were
not uncommon as bad guys, but none of them

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:18.760
were quite like Egg Fu: a gigantic egg - yes,
a literal egg - with a face straight out of

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:23.620
the "drawing Asian faces for maximum outrage"
handbook and an accent devoid of prepositions.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:27.700
Lacking limbs, he attacked people with his
mustache, and even managed to kill both Wonder

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.800
Woman and Steve Trevor in his first appearance.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:33.700
Fortunately, Queen Hippolyta
brought them back to life with Amazon technology.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:35.920
It's nice to know that’s an option when
things go badly.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:40.120
As for Egg Fu, he went the Humpty Dumpty route,
but has been brought back again and again

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:41.000
over the years.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:45.320
Recent creators have made an effort to make
the character not so over the top in 60s stereotypes,

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:47.460
but we’re not sure he’s worth the effort.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:51.620
At the very least, we can be confident he
won't be in a Wonder Woman movie anytime soon.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.100
The embarrassing TV pilot in 1967

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:59.580
With the popularity of Batman in the 1960s,
producer William Dozier [DOE-zhe-ur] ]started

00:03:59.599 --> 00:04:03.300
looking for other DC superheroes to bring
to television, and Wonder Woman seemed like

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:04.420
an obvious choice.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:08.620
With writer Stanley Ralph Ross and director
Leslie H. Martinson, both of whom worked on

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:12.660
Batman, he created a five-minute Wonder Woman
pilot starring Ellie Wood Walker in the title

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:13.160
role.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:17.340
Diana Prince is portrayed as a mousey klutz
living with her mother, who is definitely

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:21.190
not the Queen of the Amazons, and much of
the pilot consists of Walker posing in front

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:22.800
of a mirror wishing she was more beautiful.

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:27.280
"And who thinks she has the beauty of Aphrodite"

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:33.620
The 
whole thing feels sexist and unappealing,

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:37.420
and Wonder Woman fans should give thanks that
only five minutes of it were ever made.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.960
The embarrassing TV pilot in 2011

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:49.100
After another failed pilot starring Cathy
Lee Crosby failed to catch on in 1974, the

00:04:49.101 --> 00:04:53.030
third effort to bring Wonder Woman to television
with star Lynda Carter was finally successful

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:53.880
the following year.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:57.740
But the pilot for a fourth attempt in 2011
never even made it to airwaves.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:02.100
It's nowhere near as bad as the 1967 version,
but it's certainly not good, either.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:06.400
This Wonder Woman was produced and written
by David E. Kelley, of Ally McBeal fame, with

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:10.580
Adrianne Palicki in the title role and Elizabeth
Hurley as the villainous Veronica Cale.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:14.940
In this incarnation, Wonder Woman publicly
goes by the name Diana Themyscira and runs

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:19.910
a corporation to support her costumed crimefighting,
but also has a secret identity as Diana Prince,

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:21.700
which she uses to avoid the public eye.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:25.400
Palicki has a pretty good look for Wonder
Woman, and acts the role as best she can,

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:29.520
but the costume isn’t great, and its “metal”
parts are unmistakably plastic.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:34.060
Palicki did later get to prove herself as
a superhero though, playing Bobbi Morse, a.k.a.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:36.240
Mockingbird, on Marvel's Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:38.360
Her sister Nubia

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:43.611
In 1973, superhero comics were making an effort
to introduce more black characters, but with

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:46.780
most of the books written and drawn by white
men, it didn't always go so well.

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:51.640
In Wonder Woman #204, Princess Diana meets
another warrior who claims the title of Wonder

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:54.840
Woman—a black woman named Nubia who rules
a floating island.

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:59.699
To Diana's surprise, Hippolyta reveals that
Nubia is her sister, explaining that she actually

00:05:59.699 --> 00:06:03.979
sculpted two baby girls out of different colored
clay, and the dark-skinned child was stolen

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:06.660
by the War God Mars to be used against the
Amazons.

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:11.180
Diana frees Nubia from the influence of Mars
and they become friends as well as sisters.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:15.600
However, someone at DC apparently decided
this wasn't a great idea, and Nubia quickly

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:16.600
disappeared from the book.

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:17.780
And that’s kind of a shame.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:22.540
Wonder Woman having a black woman as her sister,
or at least a close ally, has plenty of potential.

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:28.700
However, the name "Nubia" is… well… yeah,
and the whole "light clay/dark clay" aspect

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:32.360
is kinda crazy when you think about it - not
the best way to explain race.

